#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/darken.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# Function: darken()"
msgstr "# Feidhm: darken()"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/darken.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Darken by `percent` HSL-lightness points — the CSS-only mirror of ui-color-utils `darken`\n(tinycolor lowers HSL lightness). Uses relative color syntax so hue and saturation are preserved."
msgstr "Dorchaigh faoi `percent` pointí éadromachta HSL — an scáthán CSS amháin de ui-color-utils `darken`\n(tá tinycolor ag laghdú éadromacht HSL). Úsáideann sé sintéis dath coibhéiseach ionas go gcoinnítear an tón agus an sáithiú."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/darken.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "In relative `hsl()`, the `l` channel resolves to a `<number>` on the 0–100 scale — the same scale\ntinycolor's `amount` uses — so the points are subtracted directly (no `%`)."
msgstr "In relative `hsl()`, the `l` channel resolves to a `&lt;number&gt;` on the 0–100 scale — the same scale\ntinycolor's `amount` uses — so the points are subtracted directly (no `%`)."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/darken.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The base color."
msgstr "An dath bhunúsach."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/darken.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "### percent?"
msgstr "### percent?"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/darken.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Lightness points to subtract (default `10`, matching tinycolor's default)."
msgstr "Pointí éadromachta le baint (réamhshocraithe `10`, ag teacht le réamhshocraithe tinycolor)."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/darken.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "An `hsl(from …)` relative-color expression."
msgstr "An léiriú relative-color `hsl(from …)`."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/lighten.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# Function: lighten()"
msgstr "# Feidhm: lighten()"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/lighten.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Lighten by `percent` HSL-lightness points — the CSS-only mirror of ui-color-utils `lighten`\n(tinycolor raises HSL lightness). Uses relative color syntax so hue and saturation are preserved."
msgstr "Éadromú faoi `percent` phointe éadromais HSL — macasamhail CSS-amharc amháin de ui-color-utils `lighten`\n(ardóidh tinycolor éadromas HSL). Úsáideann sé sintéis dath coibhéiseach ionas go gcoinnítear tón agus sáithiú."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/lighten.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Lightness points to add (default `10`, matching tinycolor's default)."
msgstr "Pointí éadromais le cuir leis (réamhshocrú `10`, ag teacht le réamhshocrú tinycolor)."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# Function: onColor()"
msgstr "# Feidhm: onColor()"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The readable foreground — black or white — for content placed *on* `surface`. This is the CSS-only\nform of InstUI's recurring `*-on-color` variants (a focus ring on a brand button, a\nprimary-inverse button's text, an icon on a coloured surface): rather than a fixed inverse token,\nit picks the contrast from the surface itself, so it stays correct as the surface changes."
msgstr "An tosaigh-inléite — dubh nó bán — do ábhar curtha *ar* `surface`. Is é seo foirm CSS-aonair na leaganacha athfhillteach `*-on-color` de InstUI (slabhra fócas ar chnaipe branda, téacs cnaipe primary-inverse, íocón ar dhromchla daite): in áit token inverse seasta, roghnaíonn sé an codarsnacht ón dromchla féin, agus mar sin fanann sé ceart agus é ag athrú."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "It reads the surface's OKLCH lightness through relative color syntax and snaps it to `0` (black) or\n`1` (white) at `threshold` using the `calc(… * infinity)` clamp trick — no JS, no fixed hex."
msgstr "Léann sé éadromacht OKLCH an dromchla trí shintéis dath rélatíf agus gleasann sé chuig `0` (dubh) nó `1` (bán) ag `threshold` ag baint úsáide as an bhfocal-clamp `calc(… * infinity)` — níl JS, níl hex seasta ann."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "### surface"
msgstr "### surface"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The background colour content sits on (literal, `var(--token)`, or a nested helper)."
msgstr "An dath cúlra ar choinneáiltear an t-ábhar air (litriúil, `var(--token)`, nó cúntóir shinsearach)."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "### threshold?"
msgstr "### threshold?"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "OKLCH lightness (0–1) above which the surface counts as \"light\" (default `0.62`)."
msgstr "Éadromacht OKLCH (0–1) os a chionn a mheastar éilíonn an dromchla mar “éadrom” (réamhshocraithe `0.62`)."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "An `oklch(from …)` expression resolving to black or white."
msgstr "Nód `oklch(from …)` a réitíonn go dubh nó bán."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/overlayColors.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# Function: overlayColors()"
msgstr "# Feidhm: overlayColors()"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/overlayColors.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Flatten `overlay` (at `percent`% strength) over an opaque `base` — a CSS-only stand-in for\nui-color-utils `overlayColors`. That helper source-over-composites two RGBA colors into one opaque\nresult; the common case (a translucent tint over a solid surface) is exactly a two-color\n`color-mix()`. General RGBA-over-RGBA compositing can't be a single CSS color, so this covers the\nopaque-base case only."
msgstr "Bain `overlay` (ag `percent`% neart) thar `base` dothuartha — ionadach CSS-amháin do ui-color-utils `overlayColors`. Déanann an cúntóir sin dhá dhath RGBA a chomhcheangal (source-over) isteach i dtorthaí dothuartha amháin; is é an cás coitianta (tint trédhearcach thar dromchla dlúth) díreach `color-mix()` dhá-dath. Ní féidir comhdhéanamh ginearálta RGBA-thar-RGBA a chur i ndath aonair CSS, mar sin clúdaíonn seo ach an chás bunús dothuartha."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/overlayColors.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The opaque background color."
msgstr "An dath cúlra dothuartha."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/overlayColors.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "### overlay"
msgstr "### overlay"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/overlayColors.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The color laid over it."
msgstr "An dath atá curtha air."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/overlayColors.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "How much of `overlay` shows through, 0–100 (default `50`)."
msgstr "Cé mhéad de `overlay` a léirítear tríd, 0–100 (réamhshocraithe `50`)."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# colors"
msgstr "# colors"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`@pantoken/plugin-colors` — CSS-only color math that mirrors the InstUI `@instructure/ui-color-utils`\nhelpers (`alpha`, `darken`, `lighten`, `overlayColors`)."
msgstr "`@pantoken/plugin-colors` — matamaitic dathanna CSS-amháin a léiríonn an InstUI `@instructure/ui-color-utils`\nfheidhmeanna cúnta (`alpha`, `darken`, `lighten`, `overlayColors`)."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "InstUI computes those at build time with `tinycolor2` against concrete hex values. pantoken emits\n`var(--instui-*)` references that resolve in the browser (often through `light-dark()`), so the\nmath has to happen in CSS instead. Each helper returns a CSS color string built from\n[`color-mix()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/color_value/color-mix) and\n[relative color syntax](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_colors/Relative_colors) —\nboth Baseline modern-browser features — so a single expression tracks the token even when it's a\nscheme-dependent `light-dark()` pair. Use them wherever you'd otherwise hard-code a derived shade."
msgstr "Ríomhann InstUI iad ag am an tógála le `tinycolor2` i gcoinne luachanna hex shoiléire. Seolann pantoken tagairtí `var(--instui-*)` a réitítear sa bhrabhsálaí (go minic trí `light-dark()`), mar sin caithfidh an matamaitic tarlú i CSS ina ionad. Tugann gach feidhm chúnta sreang dath CSS tógtha ó\n[`color-mix()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/color_value/color-mix) agus\n[relative color syntax](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_colors/Relative_colors) —\nar aon ghnéithe bunlíne brabhsálaithe nua-aimseartha — mar sin rianóidh aon abairt amháin an token fiú nuair is péire `light-dark()` í atá spleách ar scéim. Bain úsáid astu in aon áit a bheadh tú, murach sin, ag códú scáth díorthaithe go Cruinn."

